After playing for a few days, I'm not finding it to be a huge
problem... I've processed the change in my head, and take greater note
of a 2 (and even a 1 if there's reason, say, I've noticed a mind-
flayer around on the level), so I'm less haplessly blundering into
things.

This isn't to say extra warnings against monsters with specific nasty
talents wouldn't be nice -- I certainly wouldn't turn my nose up at
any such things. :) But I wonder if the larger problem isn't simply
that once you make the 1-5 scale centered on 3, it only has two levels
of difficulty on which it can grade a threat level to you. So... the
higher level you get, the more the scale doesn't have enough grades to
distinguish between some widely varying threats -- say, between a
lizard and a mind-flayer (at least for an XL23 character).

This is not an invitation to make lizards more scary. ;)  But maybe a
scale of 1-7 centered on 4 or 1-9 centered on 5 would help.





